  "docText": [
    "SOLAR®",
    "Biamp Design System",
    "1.0",
    "FAB",
    "Description",
    "Floating Action Button: the single most important action on a screen, elevated above content via shadow/raised. Fixed to the content area (usually bottom-right). Use sparingly — one FAB per screen, max. Most dense B2B screens do NOT need a FAB; a primary Button in the page header works fine. Use when the primary action must remain reachable while the user scrolls.",
    "Type",
    "icon          Circular, icon-only. Use when the action is universally recognizable (plus / add, compose, scan).\nextended   Pill, icon + label. Use when the icon would be ambiguous — label clarifies (\"New project\", \"Compose\").",
    "Sizes",
    "sm (44px)    Inside constrained content areas (inspector panes, narrow columns).\nmd (56px)    Default. Full-screen primary action on mobile + desktop.\n\nHit area ≥ 44×44 (WCAG 2.5.5) — sm meets this exactly; don't go smaller.",
    "Accessibility",
    "icon type needs aria-label matching the action verb; extended type gets its name from the visible label. shadow/raised provides visual separation. Keyboard: reachable via Tab, Enter/Space activates. Focus ring via shadow/focus/default. Don't obstruct scrolling content — move above toast / snackbar stacks.",
    "Rules",
    "Do\n\n• One FAB per screen — the single primary action\n• Use extended when the icon could be ambiguous\n• Provide aria-label on icon type\n• Move above toast stacks when they appear",
    "Don't\n\n• Don't use FAB where a primary Button in the page header is fine\n• Don't stack multiple FABs — pick one\n• Don't use for secondary / tertiary actions\n• Don't hide content under the FAB — leave bottom padding"
  ],
  "pageContext": null
}
